This crate is a Rust port of github.com/dobbo-ca/cadmus at b7fac51.

src/nn/tables.rs holds the tanh and logistic lookup tables of Tesseract's src/lstm/functions.cpp
(Apache License, Version 2.0, see above), carried over from internal/nn/tables.go.

These Rust files are translations of Tesseract OCR sources (Apache License, Version 2.0, see
above), made through the Go port, and each carries a header naming its Tesseract source files:
src/nn/funcs.rs (src/lstm/functions.h); src/nn/layers.rs and src/nn/mod.rs (src/lstm: network,
plumbing, series, parallel, reversed, input, convolve, reconfig, maxpool, fullyconnected, lstm);
src/dict/mod.rs (src/dict/dict.cpp, dict.h); src/tessdata/dawg.rs (src/dict/dawg.cpp, dawg.h);
src/tessdata/network.rs (src/lstm/network.cpp, plumbing.cpp, lstm.cpp, fullyconnected.cpp,
convolve.cpp, maxpool.cpp, reconfig.cpp, input.cpp, lstmrecognizer.cpp, weightmatrix.cpp and
src/ccstruct/matrix.h); src/tessdata/recoder.rs (src/ccutil/unicharcompress.cpp, .h);
src/tessdata/unicharset.rs (src/ccutil/unicharset.cpp); src/tessdata/mod.rs (tessdatamanager.cpp,
serialis.cpp); src/recog/build.rs (src/lstm/network.cpp); src/recog/beam.rs (src/lstm/recodebeam.cpp);
src/recog/certainty.rs (src/lstm/networkio.cpp, recodebeam.cpp); src/recog/decode.rs
(src/lstm/recodebeam.cpp, lstmrecognizer.cpp); src/recog/normalize.rs (src/lstm/networkio.cpp,
input.cpp, src/ccstruct/imagedata.cpp, statistc.cpp); src/recog/words.rs (src/lstm/recodebeam.cpp,
src/ccmain/linerec.cpp, ltrresultiterator.cpp); src/recog/mod.rs (the same files).

src/imaging/scalegray.rs is a Rust translation of pixScale and the 8bpp routines it reaches, from
Leptonica 1.87.0 (src/scale1.c, src/enhance.c, src/pix2.c); the Leptonica BSD 2-Clause licence is
reproduced above.

src/nn/funcs.rs (go_exp) follows Go's amd64 math.Exp (src/math/exp_amd64.s) and go_log follows
Go's amd64 math.Log (src/math/log_amd64.s, log.go, from FreeBSD's e_log.c, notice below),
src/imaging/gomath.rs is Go's pure math.Sin, math.Cos, math.Tan and trigReduce (src/math/sin.go,
tan.go, trig_reduce.go; the latter derived from Cephes, Copyright Stephen L. Moshier), and
src/tessdata/goquote.rs follows Go's strconv.Quote and IsPrint (src/strconv/quote.go), so that
results equal the Go library's. They are reproduced under the Go licence:

